    title: 'The related-works ledger: every extra listed, three layers',
    statement:
      "Every related work of a series we hold — recap, compilation, special, OVA, film — is a ROW in watch_order_entries (origin 'halo'; lib/related-works.ts, sync-related-works.ts) with its identity (anilist_id), the relation that reached it, its kind (T29's format axis: movie / ova / special / recap), a STANDING in the episode vocabulary (canon | mixed | filler — never a third 'essential / optional / skippable' axis; the skip guide is standing + format), a derived position (after the last episode that aired before it; a ruling by AniList id in lib/rulings/watch-order-labels.ts overrides) and a note naming its bucket. THREE LAYERS, never collapsed: (1) the LEDGER lists everything (music videos and promotional entries — trailers, PVs, teasers, commercials — are ignored: listed by the census as extra_promo, never a row; character-only crossovers are listed, not fetched); (2) the NUMBERED COUNT admits only counted extras, which keep a component (N4) — a recap never becomes an integer row (N8); (3) the SERIES PAGE shows only labeled rows (N31, display_label; the app reads nothing else) — a work our sources already number into the run surfaces with a note, everything else is the sitting's decision. The BUCKET decides the standing where a rule can: SUMMARY / COMPILATION or a recap title → filler, kind recap; source ORIGINAL → filler (T25: no instrument); a character-only crossover → filler; a work adapting the owner's own instrument (the registered manga or a chain work, I41; a novel owner's instrument is the NOVEL node its own anime adapts — T25, ownerInstrumentIds) → standing PENDING — an ADAPTATION edge to one of those ids counts whatever the `source` tag says (I47, 2026-09-05) — the sitting and research decide with its chapters; another work under the extra's OWN source (adaptedNodes: a novelization is never a source) → pending and a series candidate too (a one-shot tie-in is not); a source naming no instrument node (AniList's franchise tag with no chapters behind it, a novel film without its edge, a visual-novel or game source) → held for Sean. Every writer deletes only its own origin (G57): sync-watch-order owns 'wiki', the sitting's rulings 'ruling', this ledger 'halo'; a stale ledger row is a listing (related_work_stale), a stored standing or kind that disagrees with the derivation is related_work_violation. THE RULING LAYER (Sean ruled (b)/(c), 2026-09-05): a researched standing, chapters or position lives in lib/rulings/related-works.ts keyed by the owner and the AniList id — relatedWorkStanding: a ruling beats the rule; the row keeps origin halo, the facts are ruled; every entry lands from a verdict (R1). A wiki or ruling row that names the same work ADOPTS the AniList identity instead of a second row (I46). A work NO owner reached by an in-run relation (SEQUEL / PREQUEL / SIDE_STORY / SPIN_OFF / PARENT / OTHER — AniList's label for an entry's own specials — / SUMMARY / COMPILATION) is an ALTERNATIVE ADAPTATION (I16) — the 1995 Ghost in the Shell beside SAC, the Heaven's Feel films beside every Fate entry: never in a run, attributed ONCE to the franchise base (I43), standing not a question, a series candidate when it adapts an instrument (step 2), held when the source has none (Sean ruled 2026-09-05). AMENDED 2026-09-06 (wave 6, the BSD Walking Alone verifier): a ruling keyed (series, anilist id) applies to EVERY ledger row carrying that id whatever its origin — a wiki / ruled row takes the ruled FACTS (standing, chapters, note, repairs) and keeps its own position (its fractional ruling; a ruled position there is refused and listed); a ruling matching no row is dead weight, listed as related_work_ruling_orphan (P24) until retired or its row restored. AMENDED 2026-09-07 (the Pasta seat, §12.149 — Sean with Cursor): POSITION IS WATCH ORDER, air_date IS RELEASE — two keys, never a third: air_date is the release fact and is never rewritten; position (an extra) / number (an episode) is the viewing order, 'where do I go next'. In one gap the .5 seat is the FIRST work in watch order, then .51, .52 — never the earlier release, never a .49; the writer's air-date seat is a PROPOSAL (the row's note says so) and a sourced watch slot beats it through a position ruling on the pair in lib/rulings/related-works.ts (planRuledMoves re-seats the collider in the same apply — Made in Abyss 13.5 / .51 / .52, Kinnikuman's licensor settings, Tanya's Pasta 12.5 before the film 12.51). The in-story timeline (chronology) is information on the row, never a sort; where it splits from watch order it splits one way (a work set earlier, made to be seen later — Kizumonogatari, Fate/Zero, No Regrets) and position carries the viewing order; a story_position beside position is the shape IF a franchise page ever needs a chronological sort — deferred to the franchise UI pass. A sitting reads the owner's EXISTING ledger notes before accepting a derived seat: the film's own note already held Pasta's order.",
